(7) Should ye not hear the words which . . .—Better, are not these the very words which . . . Haggai 2:5, and Zechariah 8:17, afford exactly parallel constructions. There is no need to supply any verb, such as “should ye not hear?” “should ye not do?” or “do ye not know?” LXX., rightly, οὐχοὗτοιοἱλόγοι;
The south.—District belonging to Judah (Joshua 15:21).
And the plain.—To the west of Judah (Joshua 15:33).
